### Multi-Tenant Notification Gateway — practical demonstration
### Run the API in Development first (dotnet run). Adjust @host to the URL printed in the console.

@host = http://localhost:5000

### 1) Token: Attendance backend for tenant-001 (Service + TenantAdmin)
# @name t1
POST {{host}}/api/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "attendance-service", "tenantId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111", "roles": ["Service", "TenantAdmin"], "lifetimeMinutes": 120 }

###
@t1 = {{t1.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2) Token: tenant-002 admin
# @name t2
POST {{host}}/api/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "branch-admin", "tenantId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222", "roles": ["Service", "TenantAdmin"], "lifetimeMinutes": 120 }

###
@t2 = {{t2.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3) Token: end user manager-1 of tenant-001
# @name u1
POST {{host}}/api/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "manager-1", "tenantId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111", "roles": ["TenantUser"], "lifetimeMinutes": 120 }

###
@u1 = {{u1.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4) Send — exact spec example shape (single "recipient"), with an idempotency key
# @name send
POST {{host}}/api/notifications/send
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-checkin-001

{
  "tenantId": "tenant-001",
  "recipient": { "userId": "manager-1", "phone": "+201000000000", "email": "manager@agency.gov.eg" },
  "notificationType": "attendance.late",
  "channels": ["InApp", "SignalR", "Email", "Sms"],
  "templateCode": "ATTENDANCE_LATE",
  "data": { "EmployeeName": "Ahmed", "CheckInTime": "08:30", "Date": "2026-11-22" },
  "priority": "High"
}

###
@notificationId = {{send.response.body.notificationId}}

### 5) Same request again → same notificationId, header Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST {{host}}/api/notifications/send
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-checkin-001

{
  "tenantId": "tenant-001",
  "recipient": { "userId": "manager-1", "phone": "+201000000000", "email": "manager@agency.gov.eg" },
  "notificationType": "attendance.late",
  "channels": ["InApp", "SignalR", "Email", "Sms"],
  "templateCode": "ATTENDANCE_LATE",
  "data": { "EmployeeName": "Ahmed", "CheckInTime": "08:30", "Date": "2026-11-22" },
  "priority": "High"
}

### 6) Track (wait 2–3 s): InApp Delivered, SignalR Sent, SMS = primary TransientFailure → backup Accepted
GET {{host}}/api/notifications/{{notificationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}

### 7) The user's inbox (Arabic: tenant-001 default language)
GET {{host}}/api/me/inbox
Authorization: Bearer {{u1}}

### 8) Isolation: tenant-002 cannot see tenant-001's notification → 404
GET {{host}}/api/notifications/{{notificationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{t2}}

### 9) Isolation: tenant-002 cannot open tenant-001's settings → 403
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/tenant-001/providers
Authorization: Bearer {{t2}}

### 10) Isolation: body tenantId of another tenant → 403
POST {{host}}/api/notifications/send
Authorization: Bearer {{t2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": "tenant-001", "recipient": { "userId": "x" }, "notificationType": "attendance.late", "templateCode": "ATTENDANCE_LATE", "priority": "Normal", "data": { "EmployeeName": "X", "CheckInTime": "08:00" }, "channels": ["InApp"] }

### 11) Settings overview of tenant-001 (channels, chains, quotas)
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/tenant-001/notification-settings
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}

### 12) Arabic template preview
POST {{host}}/api/tenants/tenant-001/templates/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "ATTENDANCE_LATE", "channel": "Email", "language": "Ar", "data": { "EmployeeName": "منى", "CheckInTime": "08:45", "Date": "2026-11-22" } }

### 13) Provider switch: add a new SMS provider and make it primary (no code change)
# @name newSms
POST {{host}}/api/tenants/tenant-001/providers
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "providerKey": "fake-sms", "name": "New SMS vendor", "settings": { "mode": "success" }, "secrets": { "apiKey": "first-key" }, "senderIdentity": "AGENCY" }

###
@newSmsId = {{newSms.response.body.id}}

### 14) Put it first in the chain
PUT {{host}}/api/tenants/tenant-001/channels/Sms/providers
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "providerConfigurationIds": ["{{newSmsId}}"] }

### 15) Rotate its secret → secretVersion 2, value never returned
PUT {{host}}/api/tenants/tenant-001/providers/{{newSmsId}}/secrets
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "secrets": { "apiKey": "rotated-key" } }

### 16) Reports
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/tenant-001/reports/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/tenant-001/reports/providers
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}

### 17) Dead letters
GET {{host}}/api/tenants/tenant-001/dead-letters
Authorization: Bearer {{t1}}
